PASS Insert focuses a persistent, editable blank code area
PASS Language dropdown supports Python, JavaScript, C++, Java, SQL and plain text
PASS Plain paste keeps code indentation and ignores rich HTML wrappers
PASS Long tilde fences, unknown labels and metadata are preserved
PASS Language controls follow their block after edits before it
PASS Empty imported fences stay visible and become editable on click
PASS Boundary editing protects fences, Ctrl+Enter exits, and undo restores an empty block
PASS Source and read-only modes preserve exact content
PASS Pasted literal closing fences stay inside code and undo restores original delimiters
PASS Keyboard navigation avoids invisible fences and preserves neighboring prose
PASS Unclosed fences remain editable and diagram previews keep their behavior
PASS Code remains readable in both themes with line numbers and a narrow viewport
